  <!-- WHAT IS A CP12 -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Is a Gas Safety Certificate (CP12)?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">A CP12 is the official document. A Gas Safe registered engineer issues it after the gas safety check. It is the only paper that meets the law. The <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/landlords/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safety Regulations of 1998</a> set it out.</p>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-navy" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>What a Landlord Gas Safety Certificate Confirms</h3>
        <p>A CP12 confirms that all gas appliances, pipework, flues and vents in a rental home have been checked. The check must be done by a <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe registered engineer</a>. The CP12 records the date of the check. It lists every appliance, where it sits and the result. The engineer's Gas Safe number is also on the document.</p>
        <p>The CP12 dates back to 1998. The Gas Safety Regulations of that year set it up. It is the legal standard for gas safety in rental homes. The law covers England, Scotland and Wales. A CP12 lasts 12 months. Only a Gas Safe engineer can issue one. A plumber or electrician cannot.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>Gas Safety Certificate vs Boiler Service. What Is the Difference?</h3>
        <p>A gas safety certificate is a legal check. It checks that appliances are safe. It does not clean, maintain or service the boiler. A boiler service is a maintenance check. It keeps the boiler running well. The maker needs it every year to keep the warranty valid. They are two separate things. You need both every year.</p>
        <p>You can book both on the same visit for £175. That saves time, hassle and money over booking them apart. The combined visit is our most popular pick with Liverpool landlords.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IS CHECKED -->
