  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Cheap Gas Safety Certificate Liverpool. Your Questions Answered</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Straight answers to what Liverpool landlords and home owners ask before they book.</p>
      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does a gas safety certificate cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A CP12 in Liverpool costs £80 for the first gas appliance. Extra appliances are £10 each. A combined CP12 and annual boiler service is £175 in one visit. The <a href="https://www.checkatrade.com/blog/cost-guides/gas-safety-certificate-cost/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Checkatrade average for Liverpool is £76 to £108</a>. No call-out fee. No hidden charges.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LEGAL</span>&nbsp; Is a landlord gas safety certificate a legal requirement in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Under the <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/landlords/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safety Regulations 1998</a>, every landlord in England must hold a valid landlord gas safety certificate for each rental home with gas. The CP12 must be renewed every 12 months. Landlords must give a copy to current tenants within 28 days. New tenants must get one before they move in. Miss this and the fine can hit £6,000 per property.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">SECTION 21</span>&nbsp; Does a lapsed gas safety certificate affect a Section 21 notice?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Have not served a valid CP12 to your tenant? You may be unable to serve a valid Section 21 notice. The courts have ruled gas safety checks are a legal must for a valid S21. A lapsed or unserved CP12 can stop eviction in its tracks. Yearly renewal and prompt hand-over of the CP12 to tenants are critical for any landlord who may need to rely on S21.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">RECORDS</span>&nbsp; How long do I need to keep a gas safety certificate?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Landlords must keep the CP12 record for at least two years from the date of issue. You must be able to show it to the HSE, the council or a tenant on request. We email the CP12 the same day. That creates a record with a timestamp on it. Keep all your CP12 files in one folder per property.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TENANTS</span>&nbsp; Can tenants request a copy of the gas safety certificate?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Tenants have a legal right to get a copy of the CP12. Landlords must give a copy to current tenants within 28 days of issue. New tenants must get one before they move in. If a tenant asks and gets nothing, they can report the landlord to the HSE or the council. We email the CP12 right away so you can forward it on the same day.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">RENEWAL</span>&nbsp; Is there a grace period for renewing a gas safety certificate?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. If the new check is between 10 and 12 months after the last one, the new CP12 runs from the old expiry date. The new date is not used. You keep the full 12 months of cover. Say your CP12 ends on 1 October and the new check is on 15 September. The new CP12 still runs until 1 October next year.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">DIFFERENCE</span>&nbsp; What is the difference between a gas safety certificate and a boiler service?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A CP12 is a legal safety check. It confirms all gas appliances are safe. It does not service or maintain the boiler. A boiler service is a maintenance check. It keeps the boiler running well. The maker needs it each year to keep the warranty valid. You need both every year. We do them together for £175 in one visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">FAULTS</span>&nbsp; What happens if an appliance fails the inspection?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We follow the gas industry rules for unsafe finds. The worst is an Immediately Dangerous fault. We turn off any such appliance before we leave. We send a written quote for the repair. We never start work without your go-ahead. A CP12 cannot be issued until the fault is fixed.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">SAME DAY</span>&nbsp; Can I get a same-day gas safety certificate in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes, when we have a slot. We offer same-day CP12 jobs across Liverpool and Merseyside. Call us on 0151 558 0334 to check. The digital CP12 is emailed the same day. For a gas emergency, call Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999 first.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is Gas Safe registered. Verify us at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. The law says only a Gas Safe engineer can issue a CP12. All our CP12 jobs are done by our engineers. We never use subs.</p></div></details>
